      "message": "I looked a bit more into this. It looks like [PacketSocketAddress already exists](https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:libcore/luni/src/main/java/android/system/PacketSocketAddress.java), and most of the boiler plate exists from the [exisiting recvfrom / recvmsg implementations](https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:libcore/luni/src/main/native/libcore_io_Linux.cpp;l\u003d644)\n\nMaybe it would just be easier to extend either recvfrom or recvmsg to support passing a PacketSocketAddress?",
